From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: airoha: hardcode the build tag in the boot banner

CONFIG_LOCALVERSION is rewritten by the OpenWrt kconfig merge, so it never
reached the built kernel and "uname -r" stayed plain "5.4.215".  Emit the tag
literally instead; bump it on every release so the boot log unambiguously
identifies the running kernel.

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-11 12:24:40.474100930 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-11 12:24:40.474100930 +0800
@@ -3,7 +3,6 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2024 AIROHA Inc
  * Author: Lorenzo Bianconi <lorenzo@kernel.org>
  */
-#include <linux/utsname.h>
 #include <linux/bitfield.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
@@ -3139,7 +3138,7 @@
 	 * that failed to update the kernel becomes obvious at a glance
 	 * instead of needing an image comparison.
 	 */
-	pr_info("AIROHA-BUILD: %s\n", init_uts_ns.name.release);
+	pr_info("AIROHA-BUILD: 5.4.215-rb209\n");
 
 	eth = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*eth), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!eth)
